Vista: the OpenGL driver linked without its unused code. LLVM's static C++ runtime holds a
reference to TryAcquireSRWLockExclusive, which Vista lacks, in a function nothing calls;
discarding unused sections removes it (as patch 0100 does for the Direct3D driver).

--- a/src/gallium/targets/wgl/meson.build
+++ b/src/gallium/targets/wgl/meson.build
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 # Copyright © Microsoft Corporation
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
 
-gallium_wgl_link_args = []
+gallium_wgl_link_args = ['-Wl,--gc-sections']
 
 wgl_def = custom_target(
   'gallium_wgl.def',
